{"uncertainty": 0.25, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "Root cause of the uart_tx regression failure: hold register reloaded while a frame is in flight", "summary": "Serves [requirement:req-d10c4df532]. Observed: triage reproduced the failure under icarus, with 1 of 4 checks failed and $finish reached at 546000 [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.triage.e2] [run:run-0002]. VeriTriage classified the log as unknown_failure at 30% confidence, with 'Likely RTL bug' as its top hypothesis [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.triage.e1] [run:run-0001]. That low-confidence result was treated as one candidate, not as a conclusion.\n\nDefect: the approved RTL [artifact:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.a1] has an unconditional `if (start) hold <= data;` before the `case (state)` statement, so it runs in every state. The same file's header states the contract: 'A start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored.' The IDLE branch already loads `hold` when a frame begins, so the extra statement adds nothing for a legal start. Its only effect is to overwrite `hold` during START, DATA or STOP.\n\nCausality: the defect causes a fault and then a failure. A start pulse arrives mid-frame. On that clock edge `hold` takes the new byte, which is the fault. The state machine keeps sending, and DATA reads `hold[bit_idx + 1]` for every bit after that edge. So the serial byte becomes a mix of the old and new data, and a byte-level check fails. The failing check marks where the fault becomes visible, which is up to several bit periods after the bad write.\n\nIncorrectness: the statement breaks the documented ignore-while-busy contract for any data value and at any point in the frame, not only in this test. Proposed fix, which is not done or checked here: delete the statement outside the case and keep the load inside IDLE.\n\nCompeting hypotheses, ranked, with what would refute each:\n(1) rtl_bug, selected. Refuted if the repro testbench, which drives one mid-frame start pulse, passed on this RTL, or failed in the same way on RTL with the out-of-case load removed.\n(2) testbench_bug, rejected on reading. The repro's expected values come from the 8N1 contract in the RTL header, not from simulator output. A wrong expectation would also fail with no mid-frame pulse; the repro's second frame, sent from idle, is expected to pass. Still open: the upstream regression testbench content is not available to me, so I cannot rule out that its failing check is a different one.\n(3) infrastructure, judged unlikely. The run built, reached $finish and printed per-check counts [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.triage.e2]. That points to a functional mismatch, not a tool or build fault. A clean rebuild has not been done.\n(4) spec_ambiguity, rejected. The header clause states the busy behaviour explicitly. The RTL's own IDLE-only load also shows the intended design.\n\nThe RTL is approved upstream with independent review on record [evidence:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.e1]. That review applies to the RTL under investigation, not to this analysis."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/uart_tx_root_cause_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Minimal self-checking repro: start pulse while busy must be ignored", "summary": "Repro for [requirement:req-d10c4df532] against [artifact:prj-a0b3e1ca75.design-under-investigation.a1].\n\nStimulus: reset, then send 0xA5 with CLKS_PER_BIT=4. During data bit 2, pulse start for one cycle with data=0x3C.\n\nReceive: a line receiver samples each bit near mid-bit, starting from the start-bit falling edge of tx. It uses no DUT internal signals.\n\nChecks, taken from the 8N1 and ignore-while-busy contract in the RTL header:\n- idle after reset\n- busy during the frame\n- start bit\n- received byte equals 0xA5\n- stop bit\n- a second, idle-to-idle frame of 0x3C\n\nExpected result: the 0xA5 byte check fails on the RTL under investigation, because hold is reloaded mid-frame, and all checks pass on RTL that ignores the pulse. A watchdog makes sure exactly one verdict line is printed.", "entry": "uart_tx_root_cause_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001", "run-0002"], "claims": ["I did not run simulator.run or any other tool for this result. The expected fail-on-buggy / pass-on-fixed behaviour of tb/uart_tx_root_cause_tb.v comes from reading the RTL and has not been observed.", "The proposed fix (deleting the out-of-case `if (start) hold <= data;`) has not been applied or simulated.", "The plusarg name the platform uses to pass the run nonce is not stated in my inputs. The testbench tries nonce=, NONCE=, nirmaan_nonce= and NIRMAAN_NONCE=. If the platform uses another name, the verdict line will lack the nonce and the reproduction gate will reject it."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Outcome rtl_bug is based on the RTL text, its header contract, and the triage reproduction.\n\nMain residual uncertainty:\n- I have not seen the contents of the upstream regression testbench, the triage testbench, or the failing log, so I cannot confirm that their failing check is the same mechanism.\n- The repro has not yet been run by the platform's gate.\n- The nonce plusarg name is an assumption.\n\nBit-level timing of the repro: the first start is sampled at posedge P0. Data bit 2 spans P12 to P16. The injected pulse is sampled at P14, so in the buggy RTL bits 3 to 7 come from 0x3C, giving a received byte of 0x25 instead of 0xA5."}
```
=== FILE: tb/uart_tx_root_cause_tb.v ===
// Root-cause repro for uart_tx: a start pulse while a frame is in flight must
// be ignored (8N1, LSB first, CLKS_PER_BIT clocks per bit). Expected values
// come from that contract, not from any implementation's output.
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
module uart_tx_root_cause_tb;
    localparam integer CLKS_PER_BIT = 4;

    reg        clk   = 1'b0;
    reg        rst   = 1'b1;
    reg        start = 1'b0;
    reg  [7:0] data  = 8'h00;
    wire       tx;
    wire       busy;

    integer pass_cnt = 0;
    integer fail_cnt = 0;
    reg     done     = 1'b0;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;

    reg       sb;
    reg       pb;
    reg [7:0] rx_byte;

    uart_tx #(.CLKS_PER_BIT(CLKS_PER_BIT)) dut (
        .clk(clk), .rst(rst), .start(start), .data(data), .tx(tx), .busy(busy)
    );

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    task check;
        input            cond;
        input [8*56-1:0] what;
        begin
            if (cond) begin
                pass_cnt = pass_cnt + 1;
                $display("CHECK PASS: %0s", what);
            end else begin
                fail_cnt = fail_cnt + 1;
                $display("CHECK FAIL: %0s", what);
            end
        end
    endtask

    task finish_test;
        begin
            if (!done) begin
                done = 1'b1;
                $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, pass_cnt, fail_cnt);
                $finish;
            end
        end
    endtask

    // Line receiver: waits for the start-bit falling edge, then samples each
    // bit about 1.5 clocks into its period.
    task rx_frame;
        output       start_bit;
        output [7:0] byte_out;
        output       stop_bit;
        integer i;
        begin
            @(negedge tx);
            @(negedge clk);
            @(negedge clk);
            start_bit = tx;
            for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
                repeat (CLKS_PER_BIT) @(negedge clk);
                byte_out[i] = tx;
            end
            repeat (CLKS_PER_BIT) @(negedge clk);
            stop_bit = tx;
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        #200000;
        if (!done) begin
            $display("TIMEOUT: test did not complete");
            fail_cnt = fail_cnt + 1;
            finish_test;
        end
    end

    initial begin
        nonce = 0;
        if (!$value$plusargs("nonce=%s", nonce))
            if (!$value$plusargs("NONCE=%s", nonce))
                if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce))
                    if (!$value$plusargs("NIRMAAN_NONCE=%s", nonce))
                        nonce = 0;

        repeat (4) @(negedge clk);
        rst = 1'b0;
        repeat (2) @(negedge clk);
        check(tx === 1'b1 && busy === 1'b0, "idle after reset: tx high, busy low");

        // Frame 1: 0xA5, with a start pulse (data 0x3C) during data bit 2.
        fork
            rx_frame(sb, rx_byte, pb);
            begin
                start = 1'b1; data = 8'hA5;
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;
                repeat (13) @(negedge clk);
                check(busy === 1'b1, "busy high while frame 1 is in flight");
                start = 1'b1; data = 8'h3C;
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;
            end
        join
        check(sb === 1'b0, "frame 1 start bit low");
        if (rx_byte !== 8'hA5)
            $display("frame 1 byte: expected a5, got %h", rx_byte);
        check(rx_byte === 8'hA5, "frame 1 byte is a5 despite start pulse while busy");
        check(pb === 1'b1, "frame 1 stop bit high");

        wait (busy === 1'b0);
        repeat (3) @(negedge clk);

        // Frame 2: 0x3C from idle, normal operation.
        fork
            rx_frame(sb, rx_byte, pb);
            begin
                start = 1'b1; data = 8'h3C;
                @(negedge clk);
                start = 1'b0; data = 8'h00;
            end
        join
        check(sb === 1'b0, "frame 2 start bit low");
        if (rx_byte !== 8'h3C)
            $display("frame 2 byte: expected 3c, got %h", rx_byte);
        check(rx_byte === 8'h3C, "frame 2 byte is 3c");
        check(pb === 1'b1, "frame 2 stop bit high");

        wait (busy === 1'b0);
        repeat (2) @(negedge clk);
        check(tx === 1'b1, "line idle high after frame 2");

        finish_test;
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
